Forecasting Methodology
Objective
- The forecasting component extends historical sales patterns into future periods to provide a quantitative planning baseline.
Approach
- The project uses Tableau's built-in forecasting functionality on the historical sales time series.
- The forecast is based on the observed historical series and should be interpreted in the context of:
Trend
- Recurring seasonal behavior
- Historical variation
- The selected time aggregation
Business Use
Forecast results can support:
- Inventory planning
- Workforce planning
- Capacity preparation
- Sales target setting
- Seasonal readiness
Important Limitation
A forecast is not a guarantee of future sales. Unexpected operational, economic, promotional, supply or demand changes can cause actual sales to differ from the projected series.
